---
import ReferenceLayout from '../layouts/ReferenceLayout.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/url';
---
<ReferenceLayout
  title="Sources"
  description="Which sources RadMage Finance relies on, in what order of preference, and how citations and verification dates are shown."
  lead="Every factual statement on RadMage Finance links to its source. This page explains which sources are used and how they are cited."
  updated="2026-11-15"
>
  <h2>Order of preference</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Primary legal texts.</strong> Statutes, regulations and official rulemaking documents.</li>
    <li><strong>Official publications and data.</strong> Material from the government agencies and central banks responsible for the subject.</li>
    <li><strong>Research and reporting.</strong> Peer-reviewed research and established news organizations, for context and always attributed.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Promotional, anonymous or unverifiable material is not used to support a fact.
  </p>

  <h2>How citations work</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Each citation names the publisher, the title of the document, its date, and a link to the original.</li>
    <li>Facts that can change, such as limits, rates or legal status, also show the date they were last verified.</li>
    <li>Quotations are exact and link to where they appear.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Data and reuse</h2>
  <p>
    Data and material from other publishers are used only where their terms allow it, with
    the attribution they require.
  </p>

  <h2>Sources by page</h2>
  <p>
    Each lesson and calculator lists its own sources at the end of the page. A combined list
    will appear here as lessons and calculators are published.
  </p>
  <p>
    Spotted a source that is wrong or out of date? See <a href={href('corrections/')}>Corrections</a>.
  </p>
</ReferenceLayout>
